            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0669" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/11916: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-15T17:00:00+03:00">November 15, 1941—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 16—8:21 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1929. The Soviet press reports that Litvinov has been appointed an Assistant
                    People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs and that Oumanski has been appointed a
                    member of the Collegium of the <pb facs="0670" n="658" xml:id="pg658"/> People’s
                    Commissariat for Foreign Affairs. Oumanski has also been made director of
                    Tass.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
